  "review_findings_fixed": [
    "Automatic authority requires an explicit structured runtime or BackupRetention grant and retains ordinary message expiry; status reports blocked authority and fresh resume renews citation",
    "Scheduled scans obtain host capacity, skip drain/maintenance, and use unique lease occurrence IDs even when configuration resets counters",
    "Scratch archive removal keeps canonical journal unchanged and refuses unique content; durable receipts precede deletion and bind exact source/survivor inode identities",
    "Parent directory fsync after removal receipt-directory creation and on source-already-absent retry closes power-loss durability gaps",
    "CLI default interval changed from 24h to 1h because default 24h message authority expires before the first 24h run; added default-value assertion and reran affected race tests plus real-provider dogfood",
    "Final dogfood checks the post-retention host ledger Pool holders/waiters and matching releases, not only earlier workflow lease audit"
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Automatic retention manages existing local plane backups only; it creates no backups and schedules no replication. One interval policy per instance; no calendar cron expression or multiple retention policies.",
    "Normal authorization expiry applies (default 24h); automatic pruning blocks when its grant expires or is removed, until an operator resumes with fresh authority.",
    "Interrupted running claims block after restart. Partial plane-backup deletion remains fail-closed and needs operator investigation; no force recovery is added.",
    "Historical job coverage and monotonic replication source pins can exceed keep. No unpin API is provided.",
    "Scratch-archive cleanup only removes exact noncanonical duplicates of the CURRENT completed cleanup archive. Unique old backups, incomplete attempts, arbitrary orphans, canonical last copies and Git refs are preserved.",
    "Offline archive cleanup uses local filesystem ownership plus explicit apply and reviewed digest; it does not trust expired authorization messages from a deleted instance. Same-user malicious filesystem mutation remains outside the ownership contract.",
    "Native and real-provider network effects stay within disposable localhost adapter/replica fixtures. No vendor-specific remote retention service or credential manager is installed.",
    "Formal proofs cover production predicates and bounded scheduling/removal models, not full filesystem, Dolt, HTTP, Git or provider internals."
  ],
